          "source_quote": "ἀνακιρνάμενοι γὰρ ταῖς ψυχαῖς, ὅπως τις τῆς αὐτοῦ σωτηρίας ἀμελήσῃ, ἐνθυμήσεις πρὸς ἃ βούλονται ὑποβάλλουσιν εἰς τὸν ἑκάστου νοῦν.",
          "english_quote": "For by blending themselves with souls, the demons suggest to each person’s mind thoughts directed toward whatever they wish, so that the person neglects their own salvation.",
          "issue": "All the meaning is represented, but the purpose clause has been moved from between the blending and the suggestion of thoughts to the sentence’s end. This does not satisfy the express requirement to preserve clause order.",
          "suggested_revision": "Restore the purpose clause before the suggestion of thoughts, for example: “For the demons, blending themselves with souls so that a person may neglect their own salvation, suggest to each person’s mind thoughts directed toward whatever they wish.” This replacement requires fresh review.",
